 \textbf{Finally, we strengthened the discussion of external validity.} Point observations and regional reanalysis have different spatial supports, and ERA5-target skill cannot automatically be interpreted as gauge-forecast skill. The label experiment covers one station and one model class without station-specific inputs or tuning, multi-station training, or deep-model retraining. The hourly station documentation does not specify the exact accumulation window; zero-hour alignment was adopted after a small $\pm1$-hour shift check, which does not prove that window. All 26,300 matched observations have rainfall indicator 111, defined in the source header as ``investigation required; there is no indicator-0 (``satisfactory) subset on which to perform the proposed sensitivity analysis. We neither infer the cause nor assume the values are necessarily erroneous. Dublin Airport is one exploratory point reference; Casement Aerodrome also has long-term hourly records, and we did not implement full-network validation or construct an independent station/radar target matched to the 25-grid-point regional support. We also distinguish within-reanalysis and observational validation in relation to \citet{https://doi.org/10.1029/2026JH001291}. Conclusions are restricted to ERA5-derived regional-mean precipitation over Dublin, and the observational checks do not establish ERA5 as a general substitute for local observations.}
 
