 \RevisedExcerpt{The experimental target is ERA5-derived regional-mean precipitation over Dublin, assessed within a common multivariate reanalysis framework rather than as a station-specific operational forecast. ERA5 supplies a long, temporally continuous record of meteorological fields on a common grid, supporting consistent construction of predictors and targets \citep{hersbach2020era5}. This describes the scope and methodological rationale of the present comparison, not evidence that reanalysis precipitation is more accurate than gauge observations. \citet{otero2023intercomparison} likewise used ERA5 predictors and precipitation fields for an architecture intercomparison, but their European daily contemporaneous modelling task differs from our six-hour-ahead hourly target. ERA5 precipitation is a model-generated estimate; consistency within its framework does not establish accuracy against independent rainfall observations.}
