 \AuthorResponse{We thank the reviewer for this suggestion. We have added the Copernicus European Regional Reanalysis (CERRA) to the reanalysis literature in Section~2 (Related work), citing \citet{ridal2024cerra}. The added text states that CERRA provides reanalysis data over Europe at a horizontal resolution of 5.5~km, finer than the global ERA5 reanalysis. It also notes that \citet{ridal2024cerra} reported improvements over ERA5 for several near-surface variables. The present study uses ERA5 for both predictors and target precipitation; it does not compare the precipitation forecasting performance of CERRA and ERA5, and we do not infer that the finer resolution of CERRA would improve the regional forecasts evaluated here. Regarding satellite products, Section~2 already discusses two evaluations of satellite-based precipitation estimates \citep{palharini2021assessment,kumar2025long}, which show that their performance depends on location, terrain and rainfall intensity.}
 
